'' A SAME-TYPE ASSIGNMENT OVER A TYPE WHOSE ONLY 'operator let' CONVERTS is a copy. Fx
'' declares 'let( byval v as double )' and 'cast( ) as double'; PickCtor, asked for the
'' let taking an Fx, found that one THROUGH THE CAST, and lowering passed the source's
'' ADDRESS as the double -- 's = p + q' stored -9223372036854775808 (the book's
'' ch12/fixedpoint.tiko), and 'this.f = o' over a byref Fx was rejected by clang. See
'' SameTypeLet_ in src/mir/lowerassign.bas.
''
'' A goldenrun.sh differential: built and run by fbc-modern 1.20 and by tiko, the two
'' outputs are byte-identical (measured 2026-10-10).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/driver/src/let-same-type-cast.bas -o tests/driver/letsametypecast.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/letsametypecast.exe
'' RUN: tests/driver/letsametypecast.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: sum 300
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: copy 100
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: member 200
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: let 1250
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
